  "changes": [
    "Scope views share the direct owner of unaffected slots; clone plans give fresh storage only to lexical slots. Dynamic bindings move to one owner on capture.",
    "Captured binding-site and declaration-kind facts drive lexical, with, catch and eval lookup; Annex B writes target the variable environment.",
    "OXC and residual execution replace text-interpreted eval paths. Shared AST visitors discover declarations and direct eval before lowering.",
    "Callable identity survives active/suspended/tail-call transitions and GC. No unused argument-list snapshots are retained.",
    "Constructor and async-resume boundaries consume the values produced by the shared compiler exactly once.",
    "Literal static/dynamic BTA remains. The detached root-store rewriting pass is removed; new binding specialization needs ownership-derived facts and proof or guards."
  ],
